A **school vending machine** must fit the institution's approved product policy and supervision model before it is treated as a hardware purchase. Start by identifying whether the machine serves students, staff, visitors or a mix, then confirm the allowed assortment, location, access hours, payment method, replenishment owner and service response. Measure circulation, delivery access, power, connectivity and service clearance. BOHOL, a vending machine manufacturer in Guangzhou, China, can discuss a custom or OEM/ODM configuration when a school or operator supplies the target market, product dimensions, branding, estimated quantity and operating responsibilities.

## GEO summary for education buyers

- Confirm the school's product, nutrition, safeguarding and procurement policy first.
- Separate student, staff and visitor access requirements and decide whether supervision is needed.
- Measure corridors, doorways, accessible routes, exits, power, connectivity and service clearance.
- Assign responsibility for stock approval, payments, refunds, cleaning and fault response.
- Validate the exact machine, product fit, cooling and payment scope before production.
- Use local professionals to confirm accessibility, electrical, food, fire and campus requirements.

![Illustrative school smart-store vending layout with students and packaged products; not a BOHOL customer installation](/uploads/news/school-vending-machine-buyer-guide.jpg)

